classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: rate
Nonnegative target events per second; default 1. Zero is silent.
argument:: correction
Nonnegative log-intensity reduction per event; default 1. Zero gives a constant-rate Poisson approximation.
argument:: maxRate
Nonnegative explicit intensity ceiling in events/second; default 20000.
argument:: seed
Init-rate local PCG32 seed. Zero derives a seed from the parent Synth; nonzero is reproducible. Reset restores the original seed.
argument:: reset
Rising edge clears z and restores the seed. Reset takes priority over event generation.
returns:: Exactly two outputs: [trigger, preEventIntensity]. Triggers are binary.

method:: kr
Control-rate version: one calculation spans the full control block. Event outputs last one block.

instancemethods::

examples::

subsection:: Minimal rhythm

Hear stochastic spacing immediately.

code::
(
{ Decay2.ar(SelfCorrectingTrig.ar(6, 1.5)[0], 0.001, 0.04) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

subsection:: Intensity recovery

Watch pressure fall after events and recover during silence.

code::
(
{ SelfCorrectingTrig.kr(3, 2, seed: 21)[1].poll(10) }.play
)
::

subsection:: Inhibition versus excitation

Left clusters; right spaces events. Both sides use the same sound and roughly six events per second.

code::
(
{
    var events = [HawkesTrig.ar(2, 8, 12, seed: 10)[0], SelfCorrectingTrig.ar(6, 1.5, seed: 11)[0]];
    SinOsc.ar(700, 0, Decay2.ar(events, 0.001, 0.05) * 0.08)
}.play
)
::
